<phyphox version="1.14" locale="en">
  <title>Probe 2: formulas and their functions work</title>
  <category>Probes</category>
  <description>
        Diagnostic. Takes ten seconds and tells you one thing: whether the formula parser accepts the functions everything else relies on

        Run the probes in order. The FIRST one that fails to import, or shows nothing, names the feature your phyphox version will not do - which turns "none of it works and I have no idea why" into a single specific problem.
    </description>

  <data-containers>
    <container size="64">raw</container>
    <container>avg</container>
    <container>probe</container>
  </data-containers>

  <input>
    <sensor type="accelerometer" rate="0">
      <output component="abs">raw</output>
    </sensor>
  </input>

  <views>
    <view label="Result">
      <value label="Should equal the acceleration" unit="m/s^2" size="3" precision="4">
        <input>probe</input>
      </value>
      <info label="This uses sqrt, cos, acos, max, min, round and abs in one expression, and the added terms are all zero, so the answer must equal plain acceleration - about 9.8 standing still. A blank or a wrong number means one of those functions is not supported, and several experiments depend on them."/>
    </view>
  </views>
  <analysis sleep="0.2">
    <average>
      <input as="buffer" clear="false">raw</input>
      <output as="average">avg</output>
    </average>
    <formula formula="sqrt([1]*[1])+0*cos(0)+0*acos(1)+0*max([1],0)+0*round(1.4)+0*abs(-1)+0*min([1],99)">
      <input>avg</input>
      <output>probe</output>
    </formula>
  </analysis>

  <export>
    <set name="Probe">
      <data name="value">probe</data>
    </set>
  </export>
</phyphox>
